{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "צהר", :translit "tzohar", :gloss "window / skylight"} {:he "אור האבן", :translit "or ha-even", :gloss "light of the stone"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "צהר", :b "אור האבן"}], :frame {:text "The word צהר in Genesis 6:16 is understood by Rashi (Genesis 6:16, citing Tanhuma) as referring either to a skylight or a luminous precious stone. The Ba'al HaTurim compresses this interpretive range by showing that the word itself encodes 'light of the stone.'", :sources ["Rashi Genesis 6:16" "Tanhuma Noach 11"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ושלשים", :translit "u-sheloshim", :gloss "and thirty"} {:he "ושלשים יסעו", :translit "u-sheloshim yisa'u", :gloss "and thirty thousand traveled"} {:he "תעשה", :translit "ta'aseh", :gloss "you shall make"} {:he "ואני סמך ואני לתעשה", :translit "va-ani samakh va-ani le-ta'aseh", :gloss "and I supported 'and I' to ta'aseh"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ושלשים"]} {:kind :other, :note "The Masoretic pair of ושלשים occurrences is read as a hint to the formation and salvific merit of the tribal banners."}], :frame {:text "Numbers 2 describes the Israelites encamped and traveling by tribal banners (degel) in formation around the Tabernacle. Rashi (Genesis 6:14) cites Bereishit Rabbah 31:10 in the name of Rabbi Yochanan that the planks of the ark required divine assistance to be cut, since Noah lacked the skill. The phrase תעשה אתה (you shall make) is read there as God saying: you do your part and I will assist. Ba'al HaTurim applies this pattern to Genesis 6:16.", :sources ["Numbers 2" "Rashi Genesis 6:14" "Bereishit Rabbah 31:10"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "צהר", :a-value 295, :b "אור האבן", :b-value 265, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ושלשים"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ושלשים", :refs ["Genesis 5:5" "Genesis 6:15" "Genesis 6:16" "Genesis 11:12" "Genesis 11:16" "Genesis 11:20" "Genesis 25:17" "Exod